          "text": "Brain fog is everyday language for slowed thinking, weaker focus, or mental effort that costs more than it used to \u2014 a symptom description, not a diagnosis by itself."
        },
        {
          "id": "brain_fog_pathway",
          "text": "Siya\u2019s brain fog guide connects fatigue, preventive care, and related labs (CBC, TSH, B12, ferritin, vitamin D). ADHD is one possible related entity, not the destination. Primary care is the starting frame."
        }
      ],
      "note": "Symptom-first. Never answer brain fog with an ADHD screening CTA."
